  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5fb2c591-3349-48b2-91c9-94be7b027448-9894601.PNG\" style=\"width: 474px; height: 105px;\" /></p><p>Dichromate oxidises to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;in acidic medium according to the reaction.</p><p>In dichromate, chromium is in +6 oxidation state and on the right hand side we have Cr in +3 state. So, the change is from +6 to +3 in acidic medium.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
